__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Named Docker volumes are managed by compose, but a bind-mount misconfiguration
# can leave real data directories behind. results/ is deliberately NOT ignored:
# it is the record of the run, and dataset.json now carries the timestamp anchor
# that every later phase reuses.
/prom-data/
/pg-data/

# Rendered from blog/post.md by blog/publish_wordpress.py --dry-run.
blog/post.html

# Grafana Cloud credentials. The template next to it is committed; this copy is not.
/monitoring/.env.monitoring

# Written by the harness as each phase samples, read by the Alloy textfile
# collector. A measurement in progress, not an input to anything. The
# directory itself IS committed (via .gitkeep): Docker creates a missing
# bind-mount source as root, and then the runner user cannot write the samples
# into it. The write failure is swallowed, so the symptom is a dashboard that
# is simply empty.
/monitoring/textfile/*.prom
/monitoring/textfile/*.tmp
